{"diagnosis": "Trace shows TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 with tohost FAIL 0xdead, meaning no fetch ever completed versus expected advancing fetches. Line 373 holds mem_xfer low because it is `&& (mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && mem_do_rinst)` instead of masking that case, so mem_done/mem_la_read never assert. This single gating inversion stalls all instruction fetch, matching zero max_addr.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -372,4 +372,4 @@
 	wire mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word = COMPRESSED_ISA && mem_la_firstword && prefetched_high_word && !clear_prefetched_high_word;
-	assign mem_xfer = (mem_valid && mem_ready) && (mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && mem_do_rinst);
+	assign mem_xfer = (mem_valid && mem_ready) && !(mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && mem_do_rinst);

 	wire mem_busy = |{mem_do_prefetch, mem_do_rinst, mem_do_rdata, mem_do_wdata};
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead) with progress max_addr != 0x00000000 and no TRAP: no progress"}

